WEBVTT

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:14.510
<i>GeGeGe no Kitaro</i>

00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:17.760
Summon <i>kijin</i>!

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:20.680
<i>On!</i>

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:33.740
<i>The world you see isn't all there is.</i>

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.660
<i>There are things you can't see.</i>

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:40.410
<i>See? In the darkness behind you...</i>

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:00.310
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:00.310
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:04.230
<i>asa wa nedoko de gu gu gu</i>

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:04.230
<i>Slumbering in bed in the morning</i>

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:08.940
<i>tanoshiina tanoshiina</i>

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:08.940
<i>It's so fun, it's so fun</i>

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:12.730
<i>obakenya gakkou mo</i>

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:12.730
<i>Ghosts don't have school</i>

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:16.610
<i>shiken mo nannimo nai</i>

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:16.610
<i>Or tests or anything</i>

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:21.410
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:21.410
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:25.000
<i>minna de utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:25.000
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:29.210
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:29.210
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:33.090
<i>yoru wa hakaba de undoukai</i>

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:33.090
<i>Sports festivals in the graveyard at night</i>

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:37.970
<i>tanoshiina tanoshiina</i>

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:37.970
<i>It's so fun, it's so fun</i>

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:42.100
<i>obake wa shinanai</i>

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:42.100
<i>Ghosts don't die</i>

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:45.520
<i>byouki mo nannimo nai</i>

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:45.520
<i>Or get sick or anything</i>

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:49.980
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:49.980
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:54.320
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:54.320
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:58.280
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:58.280
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:03.240
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:03.240
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:12.210
CELEBRATING COMPLETION OF
THE NAGATOMI DAM

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:11.190
A quarter century since planning
and construction,

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:17.320
and after protests and debates,
the Nagatomi Dam is at last complete!

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:20.220
They're now opening the floodgates!

00:02:24.930 --> 00:02:26.330
Amazing!

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:27.890
Wonderful!

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:33.630
-Pee yoo!
-My eyes are stinging!

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:38.150
What's going on?! The dam's water has
turned reddish black!

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:47.540
CHAPTER 62

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:52.520
THE FOUR GENERALS OF THE UNDERWORLD
KUROBOZU'S TRAP

00:02:59.550 --> 00:03:01.160
Apologize like you mean it.

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:01.990
Hmph!

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:05.250
Sure, whatever. I'm sorry.

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:07.250
-Why you...!
-I just apologized!

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:09.000
You really are...!

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:11.130
I'm never rescuing you again!

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:14.840
Whatever!
I can get along fine without you!

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:17.720
Fine. Then we're through.

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:19.900
Fine! Good riddance!

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:23.200
What happened with them?

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:25.010
Well...

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:29.310
Let's eat!

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:31.170
Oh, pepper...

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:39.760
They're fighting over that?

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:43.430
Super spicy mapo tofu!

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:48.540
Hot! Hot, hot, hot, hot!

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:51.020
Water!

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:54.290
Yuck, yuck, yuck, yuck, yuck, yuck!

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:56.670
Eww! It smells!

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:59.050
-Pee yoo!
-What is this?!

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:04.470
WATER

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:07.470
<i>To everyone buying bottled water.</i>

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:10.640
We're limiting two bottles per person!

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:12.480
BOTTLED WATER SOLD OUT!!

00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:15.070
We're sorry! We're very sorry!

00:04:15.070 --> 00:04:18.030
We're all sold out of water!

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:20.460
What's going on there?

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:22.130
Hey you.

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:34.250
Are you Rat Man-san?

00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:37.080
I've got a profitable proposal for you.

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:39.000
KUROBOZU

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:41.760
Are you interested?

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:43.630
Profitable?!

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:46.640
Honestly, those two.

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:50.950
Those guys cut ties
two or three times a year.

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:55.400
You know, I've been wondering.

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:59.740
Kitaro and Rat Man-san are friends, right?

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:03.410
I'm not sure they can be called that.

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:08.370
When Rat Man's really in trouble,
Kitaro always ends up saving him.

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:11.040
And they kind of make up.

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:14.890
They just do that over and over.

00:05:16.060 --> 00:05:17.520
It's from Mom...

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:22.300
What?! There's trouble with the water?

00:05:26.570 --> 00:05:29.430
UNEXPLAINED POLLUTION
FILTERING SYSTEMS INEFFECTIVE?!

00:05:29.660 --> 00:05:33.560
Water that can't be purified
by any means...

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:36.060
What happens if you still drink it?

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:41.570
It won't kill you, but it'll upset
your stomach something terrible.

00:05:41.570 --> 00:05:43.240
Dad, this is...

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:46.780
Yes. There's a possibility.

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:49.530
Kurobozu was a <i>yokai</i> that polluted water.

00:05:49.890 --> 00:05:52.250
Isn't Kurobozu one of
the Four Treasonous Generals--

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:53.660
Hey!

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:56.750
Treasonous what?

00:05:56.750 --> 00:06:03.170
Especially evil <i>yokai</i> that tried to
wipe out humanity long ago.

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:05.090
Such terrifying <i>yokai</i> exist?

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:06.300
Yeah.

00:06:06.570 --> 00:06:10.030
They were held in the underworld,
but escaped.

00:06:10.030 --> 00:06:13.470
Enma-Daio asked me to apprehend them.

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:17.060
By Enma-Daio, you mean
the one from the underworld?!

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:17.860
Yeah.

00:06:17.860 --> 00:06:22.000
If they escaped, shouldn't he
deal with them himself?

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:25.480
I guess Enma-Daio's pretty useless.

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:27.870
What is this reddish black water?!

00:06:27.870 --> 00:06:30.240
It stinks! What can we do?

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:32.910
What is the government doing?!

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:34.830
POLLUTION SPREADS ACROSS KANTO REGION

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:36.580
WATER TRUCK SHORTAGE
LACK OF SOURCE

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:38.330
NO WATER! SOMEONE HELP!

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:44.590
It seems the humans are
also investigating,

00:06:45.070 --> 00:06:49.360
but, just like us, they can't
find the source of the pollution.

00:06:50.860 --> 00:06:56.160
There aren't many records on Kurobozu,
so it's unclear.

00:06:57.120 --> 00:07:00.150
During the Ansei period
under the Tokugawa Shogunate,

00:07:00.150 --> 00:07:04.690
he polluted the wells and rivers of Edo
and killed hundreds of thousands

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:07.650
before being defeated by the Kidoshu.

00:07:08.220 --> 00:07:10.260
The Kidoshu again?

00:07:11.550 --> 00:07:14.740
Do you think he'll show up?

00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:16.930
Rei Isurugi.

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:19.500
Probably.

00:07:19.890 --> 00:07:25.440
He's been hell-bent on revenge
since his home village was burned down.

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:30.780
Kitaro!

00:07:31.610 --> 00:07:33.260
Look at this!

00:07:33.260 --> 00:07:34.140
Huh?

00:07:34.160 --> 00:07:39.580
OMACHI SHOPPING

00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:39.650
<i>So, will using this purifier
really clear up the water?</i>

00:07:39.650 --> 00:07:41.640
<i>Of course!</i>

00:07:43.250 --> 00:07:48.210
<i>Just attach the BiBiBi Cleaner I invented
to the polluted water,</i>

00:07:48.590 --> 00:07:49.900
<i>and presto!</i>

00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:56.350
<i>The reddish black water instantly
becomes delicious water.</i>

00:07:56.910 --> 00:07:58.600
<i>Go ahead!</i>

00:07:59.140 --> 00:08:01.410
<i>Are you sure it's safe?</i>

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:05.360
<i>I don't smell that ugly stench.</i>

00:08:07.690 --> 00:08:09.550
<i>Wow! This is delicious!</i>

00:08:09.550 --> 00:08:10.930
<i>Isn't it?</i>

00:08:10.930 --> 00:08:16.930
<i>We'll be renting out BiBiBi Cleaners
for a monthly fee of 500 yen!</i>

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:19.430
<i>Sign up now!</i>

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:22.060
Yes, this is BiBiBi Cleaners.

00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:23.940
300 units? Of course!

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:26.250
We have more than enough!

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:29.420
PRESIDENT'S OFFICE

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:29.530
What are you up to, Rat Man.

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:34.030
"Up to"? I'm just
working to help everyone.

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:35.530
You're lying.

00:08:35.530 --> 00:08:38.780
Hey, what's the meaning of that,
Kitaro-chan?

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:41.790
Am I causing trouble for anyone?

00:08:45.270 --> 00:08:46.790
I'm not!

00:08:47.060 --> 00:08:48.880
Am I swindling anyone?

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:50.250
I'm not!

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:54.260
And what happens if
I pull out of this business right now?

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:57.180
Without water everyone's in trouble.

00:08:57.180 --> 00:09:00.220
The country and all those
big scientists couldn't do anything.

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:05.480
Then I came and solved it!

00:09:06.040 --> 00:09:10.840
The moment the water went bad,
you invented a purifier?

00:09:12.260 --> 00:09:13.360
It's too convenient.

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:14.160
Gulp!

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:17.110
Isn't Kurobozu involved with this?

00:09:17.430 --> 00:09:20.060
Kurobozu? Who's that?

00:09:26.850 --> 00:09:30.710
Sir, it's time for you meeting with
the Prime Minister.

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:32.550
Okay! On my way!

00:09:33.150 --> 00:09:36.550
As you can see, I'm busy helping people.

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:39.550
If we're done here, feel free to leave.

00:09:45.910 --> 00:09:48.270
Was that GeGeGe no Kitaro?

00:09:48.270 --> 00:09:49.330
Yeah.

00:09:49.750 --> 00:09:51.740
Don't worry about him.

00:09:51.740 --> 00:09:56.200
So, are the purifiers in use all over?

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:57.280
Of course.

00:09:57.280 --> 00:10:00.280
Then it's about time.

00:10:02.030 --> 00:10:05.160
Oh? It's from BiBiBi Cleaners.

00:10:02.140 --> 00:10:05.060
NOTICE FROM BIBIBI CORPORATION
ABOUT THE BIBIBI CLEANER

00:10:05.480 --> 00:10:09.210
"Notice of change in usage fee

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:12.840
from 500 yen to 500,000 yen..."

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:14.300
500,000 yen?!

00:10:16.820 --> 00:10:18.300
Please don't!

00:10:18.300 --> 00:10:20.720
Then hurry up and pay!

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:23.260
F-Fine! I'll pay already!

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:25.600
MONTHLY STATEMENT
500,000 YEN

00:10:30.290 --> 00:10:33.070
I'm running a private business here.

00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:38.470
You're the ones who decided
to completely rely on me as your lifeline.

00:10:39.380 --> 00:10:44.160
The country itself could always
pay the usage fee, you know.

00:10:45.430 --> 00:10:47.500
Your whatever-nomics made you rich, right?

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:53.170
Actually, we just tweaked the statistics
to suit our needs.

00:10:53.610 --> 00:10:55.420
Oh very well.

00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:57.920
In that case, I have one request.

00:10:57.920 --> 00:11:00.070
Wh-What is it?

00:11:00.450 --> 00:11:04.760
I've always wanted to be
a Cabinet minister.

00:11:06.410 --> 00:11:09.600
Man, they said
they'll give me any position.

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:12.600
Talk about no spine or pride.

00:11:19.550 --> 00:11:21.010
NUE

00:11:49.250 --> 00:11:51.600
KUROBOZU

00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:56.110
SAND WITCH

00:11:54.130 --> 00:11:55.000
-<i>"I sense </i>yokai<i> activity."</i>
-<i>"Scratch, scratch."</i>

00:11:55.130 --> 00:11:56.000
<i>"What is this guy...?"</i>

00:11:56.110 --> 00:11:58.550
WATER STATION

00:12:03.510 --> 00:12:06.510
I know Kurobozu is involved.

00:12:06.850 --> 00:12:08.680
Where is he?

00:12:08.680 --> 00:12:09.750
I don't know.

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:11.250
I see.

00:12:14.560 --> 00:12:16.250
Where's Kurobozu!

00:12:21.240 --> 00:12:24.010
I thought you cut ties with Rat Man.

00:12:24.010 --> 00:12:26.410
Yet you're saving him.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:31.390
You know...

00:12:31.390 --> 00:12:37.130
Mana was wondering why you've been
friends with Rat Man for so long.

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:39.900
I wondered the same thing.

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:44.800
Tell me Kitaro, what is Rat Man to you?

00:12:51.180 --> 00:12:52.540
You're a stubborn one.

00:12:52.850 --> 00:12:54.560
I didn't expect that.

00:12:55.350 --> 00:13:00.550
I'm gonna rule the water to become
a Cabinet minster and then Prime Minister

00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:02.490
to prove to Kitaro...!

00:13:03.360 --> 00:13:08.060
You think a half-<i>yokai</i> like you
can change the human world?

00:13:08.060 --> 00:13:09.220
Screw you!

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:13.900
<i>If I hold out, Kurobozu may lose patience
and come looking for me eventually.</i>

00:13:13.900 --> 00:13:17.190
<i>I'm not giving up until then.</i>

00:13:17.190 --> 00:13:18.500
Very well.

00:13:22.880 --> 00:13:25.010
So much for making you talk.

00:13:26.300 --> 00:13:29.910
If you won't talk, you're useless to me.

00:13:29.910 --> 00:13:31.410
Time to disappear.

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:33.180
Summon <i>kijin</i>!

00:13:31.890 --> 00:13:33.640
ONI

00:13:40.110 --> 00:13:43.210
Disappear, half-<i>yokai</i>!

00:13:49.240 --> 00:13:50.410
Kitaro...

00:13:50.780 --> 00:13:52.770
Release Rat Man!

00:13:52.770 --> 00:13:56.980
It's indisputable that
he's working with Kurobozu!

00:13:57.540 --> 00:13:59.980
Why defend this worthless half-<i>yokai</i>?!

00:14:02.090 --> 00:14:03.980
Because he's your friend?

00:14:06.800 --> 00:14:12.350
You've defeated countless <i>yokai</i>
who've done evil.

00:14:21.900 --> 00:14:25.430
And yet, you'd let this one go?!

00:14:25.430 --> 00:14:27.110
You hypocrite!

00:14:27.110 --> 00:14:28.660
Hair Needles!

00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:36.350
Spirit Hair Chanchanko!

00:14:46.380 --> 00:14:47.780
Catchick!

00:14:47.780 --> 00:14:49.510
Wake up already!

00:14:50.300 --> 00:14:53.330
You contradict yourself,
GeGeGe no Kitaro!

00:14:53.330 --> 00:14:55.870
I know that!

00:14:56.270 --> 00:15:01.670
Rat Man really is a hopeless cause.

00:15:01.670 --> 00:15:06.670
He keeps repeating the same mistakes
and never shows signs of changing.

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:09.070
So why defend him?!

00:15:09.530 --> 00:15:13.390
Is it pity? For a half-<i>yokai</i> like him?

00:15:13.390 --> 00:15:14.620
No!

00:15:15.200 --> 00:15:19.000
A world where those like him can't live...

00:15:19.370 --> 00:15:22.840
That's what I hate the most!

00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:29.450
If Rat Man makes mistakes,
I'll be angry and punish him.

00:15:29.450 --> 00:15:30.430
But...

00:15:30.800 --> 00:15:34.950
If he suffers and shows remorse,
I'd like to forgive him.

00:15:35.890 --> 00:15:38.310
I want to be someone who can forgive!

00:15:39.810 --> 00:15:41.190
Kitaro...

00:15:46.570 --> 00:15:48.670
You're soft, GeGeGe no Kitaro!

00:15:48.670 --> 00:15:50.050
I know that!

00:15:50.050 --> 00:15:53.010
But, being unable to forgive the evil...

00:15:53.910 --> 00:15:56.850
Thinking they should all be killed...

00:15:56.850 --> 00:16:00.950
To deny those who are different
and to only allow those similar to you...

00:16:00.950 --> 00:16:03.980
To be unable to see how absurd that is...

00:16:04.590 --> 00:16:06.570
That's what I fear the most.

00:16:07.130 --> 00:16:10.990
That's right, Rei Isurugi.
People like you!

00:16:10.990 --> 00:16:12.030
Save it!

00:16:17.890 --> 00:16:19.890
Now then...

00:16:21.270 --> 00:16:27.230
Let's take care of both of you right here.

00:16:28.900 --> 00:16:30.420
Kurobozu!

00:16:39.700 --> 00:16:43.980
Rat Man is an important pawn in my plans.

00:16:43.980 --> 00:16:46.360
I can't have him die.

00:16:46.360 --> 00:16:47.440
Your plans?

00:16:47.440 --> 00:16:48.730
Nothing much.

00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:51.790
I just used up here this time.

00:16:51.790 --> 00:16:53.570
A hundred and fifty years ago,

00:16:53.570 --> 00:16:59.290
I tried to destroy the humans myself and
ended up being beaten by some dingy monks.

00:16:59.290 --> 00:17:02.410
The ones who defeated you
were the Kidoshu!

00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:04.850
Huh? The Kidoshu?

00:17:04.850 --> 00:17:08.610
As if I cared about monk factions.

00:17:10.650 --> 00:17:15.350
You don't know our name?
This isn't the one either.

00:17:15.350 --> 00:17:20.680
This time, using the mechanisms of
human society, I thought I'd control him

00:17:20.680 --> 00:17:24.390
to rule the humans from behind the scenes.

00:17:27.500 --> 00:17:28.710
Kitaro!

00:17:33.760 --> 00:17:37.490
Kurobozu! How to defeat you
has been passed down!

00:17:38.760 --> 00:17:40.370
Your weakness is...

00:17:41.640 --> 00:17:42.770
this!

00:17:45.710 --> 00:17:49.790
That's right! Your weakness is water!

00:17:50.320 --> 00:17:54.610
Ironic that a <i>yokai</i> that pollutes water
is weak against it!

00:17:55.700 --> 00:17:56.800
Just kidding.

00:18:01.160 --> 00:18:06.090
True, I was
defeated with water 150 years ago.

00:18:06.090 --> 00:18:12.020
But I guess they didn't pass down
why I was weak against water.

00:18:12.020 --> 00:18:15.720
Besides, you're fighting the wrong target.

00:18:20.350 --> 00:18:23.180
<i>"Fighting the wrong target"?</i>

00:18:26.230 --> 00:18:28.150
<i>Come to think of it, Kurobozu...</i>

00:18:30.230 --> 00:18:33.190
<i>If that's his true form, then...</i>

00:18:33.820 --> 00:18:35.070
<i>Is it...</i>

00:18:36.320 --> 00:18:37.740
<i>somewhere nearby?</i>

00:18:45.330 --> 00:18:47.180
Hey! Rat Man!

00:18:51.690 --> 00:18:53.190
Found it!

00:18:53.500 --> 00:18:56.690
Kurobozu, this picture's
your true form, isn't it?!

00:18:57.550 --> 00:18:59.030
All right!

00:18:59.030 --> 00:19:01.030
You're weak against water!

00:19:01.030 --> 00:19:03.560
Open the floodgates!

00:19:13.150 --> 00:19:16.130
Hah! Take that!

00:19:16.130 --> 00:19:18.840
Curse... you...

00:19:18.840 --> 00:19:22.140
Rat... Man...!

00:19:29.670 --> 00:19:31.100
Kurobozu!

00:19:31.830 --> 00:19:33.310
Finger Guns!

00:19:44.010 --> 00:19:45.260
Got him!

00:19:45.720 --> 00:19:48.080
Rat Man, are you okay?

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:49.710
Yes...

00:19:49.710 --> 00:19:51.790
Honestly.

00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:54.250
I hope you've learned your lesson.

00:19:54.250 --> 00:19:55.940
Yes...

00:19:56.360 --> 00:19:58.150
GeGeGe no Kitaro.

00:20:02.160 --> 00:20:06.140
I'm taking Kurobozu's soul to Enma-Daio.

00:20:06.140 --> 00:20:07.390
Go ahead.

00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:12.500
If it didn't know the Kidoshu,
it couldn't have burned our village.

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:15.230
But there won't be a next time.

00:20:15.590 --> 00:20:20.280
Hearing you spout your nonsense
made me hate you even more.

00:20:20.280 --> 00:20:22.000
What a coincidence.

00:20:22.000 --> 00:20:23.990
I hate you, too.

00:20:24.970 --> 00:20:26.220
Rei Isurugi.

00:20:40.150 --> 00:20:41.760
Apologize like you mean it!

00:20:41.760 --> 00:20:42.630
Hmph!

00:20:43.660 --> 00:20:45.350
What's that attitude?!

00:20:45.350 --> 00:20:47.520
Sure, whatever. I'm sorry.

00:20:47.520 --> 00:20:49.390
You really are...!

00:20:49.390 --> 00:20:50.730
I apologized!

00:20:50.730 --> 00:20:52.270
What is it this time?

00:20:52.270 --> 00:20:54.020
He stole a sweet bun.

00:20:54.020 --> 00:20:55.100
Seriously?

00:20:55.100 --> 00:20:56.900
Do you feel bad?!

00:20:56.900 --> 00:20:58.320
-Sure I do! Of course!
-Honestly...

00:20:58.320 --> 00:21:01.170
They never grow up, do they?

00:21:02.260 --> 00:21:06.800
Tell me Kitaro, what is Rat Man to you?

00:21:07.510 --> 00:21:09.490
Well...

00:21:09.850 --> 00:21:13.500
When it seemed like
Nanashi was going to swallow everything,

00:21:13.500 --> 00:21:16.860
I almost gave up once.

00:21:17.860 --> 00:21:20.130
The one who helped me back up

00:21:20.360 --> 00:21:22.070
was Rat Man.

00:21:24.610 --> 00:21:27.820
As far back as I can recall,
even at times like that,

00:21:28.160 --> 00:21:35.140
though he may crawl through the mud,
he still always brazenly tries to survive.

00:21:35.620 --> 00:21:38.750
It's because of him... that I...

00:21:44.130 --> 00:21:45.630
Cat-san?

00:21:46.180 --> 00:21:49.240
What's wrong? You're smirking.

00:21:49.240 --> 00:21:52.310
Huh? Nothing.

00:21:53.100 --> 00:21:54.730
All things considered...

00:21:55.640 --> 00:21:59.400
Men are... such a hassle.

00:22:14.580 --> 00:22:17.750
<i>kimi wa yume boku no yume</i>

00:22:14.580 --> 00:22:17.850
<i>You're a dream
My dream</i>

00:22:17.850 --> 00:22:21.320
<i>I'm dreaming in a dream</i>

00:22:17.880 --> 00:22:21.210
<i>yume no naka de yume miteiru</i>

00:22:21.320 --> 00:22:24.820
<i>Let's stay like this forever</i>

00:22:21.340 --> 00:22:24.720
<i>itsumade mo kono mama de imashou</i>

00:22:25.130 --> 00:22:28.300
<i>kasuka kimi ga nijimu</i>

00:22:25.130 --> 00:22:28.410
<i>You blur and begin to fade</i>

00:22:28.410 --> 00:22:35.080
<i>Don't you cry
Where did you come from?</i>

00:22:28.430 --> 00:22:35.020
<i>Don't you cry anata wa doko kara kitano?</i>

00:22:35.080 --> 00:22:39.880
<i>A masquerade
Faceless faces laugh</i>

00:22:35.140 --> 00:22:39.770
<i>kamenbutou kao no nai kao ga warau</i>

00:22:39.880 --> 00:22:42.210
<i>Hee-hee-hee</i>

00:22:39.900 --> 00:22:42.150
<i>fufufu</i>

00:22:42.210 --> 00:22:45.920
<i>In dreams, in dreams
Lost in dreams</i>

00:22:42.270 --> 00:22:45.820
<i>yume ni yume ni yume ni samayoi</i>

00:22:45.920 --> 00:22:48.260
<i>Twirling around</i>

00:22:45.940 --> 00:22:48.160
<i>kuru kuru to mawaru</i>

00:22:48.260 --> 00:22:52.560
<i>Everyone dancing, dancing
Looking for love</i>

00:22:48.280 --> 00:22:52.490
<i>dare mo odoru odoru ai wo sagashite</i>

00:22:52.560 --> 00:22:59.330
<i>RONDO, spin, spin
Dream, dream</i>

00:22:52.620 --> 00:22:59.330
<i>RONDO mawareyo maware yume yume</i>

00:23:01.500 --> 00:23:05.610
<i>Dad, a bamboo spirit is hurting humans.</i>

00:23:05.610 --> 00:23:07.530
<i>Huh? Wally Wall...?</i>

00:23:07.530 --> 00:23:10.280
<i>Next time on GeGeGe no Kitaro</i>

00:23:10.280 --> 00:23:12.780
<i>"The Star Festival of Love
The Yokai Flower"</i>

00:23:12.780 --> 00:23:15.470
<i>The door to the unseen world opens...</i>
